Feature: the reference documentation carries each paragraph once

  # One botched documenter insertion (commit 7fa17fecd, 2026-07-24) wedged 287
  # copies of the same BL-607 paragraph between almost every paragraph in the
  # last third of docs/reference/Specification.MD. 286 copies remain, spanning
  # lines 2486-3358 with 159 real paragraphs interleaved among them, and 284 of
  # the 286 carry a quote-mangled `role_ask.bb --options` example - so the
  # majority variant is the WRONG text. Nothing in the tree looks for repeated
  # documentation prose, so it went unnoticed for 17 days while every later
  # documenter pass edited around it.

  # BL-873 docs-duplicate-paragraph-01
  Scenario: the real docs tree repeats no substantial paragraph
    Given the scanned docs tree is the real docs directory
    When the duplicate-paragraph guard scans that tree
    Then it reports zero repeated paragraphs

  # BL-873 docs-duplicate-paragraph-02
  Scenario: a repeated paragraph is named until a single copy remains
    Given a scanned docs tree whose markdown repeats one substantial paragraph
    When the duplicate-paragraph guard scans that tree
    Then it names that paragraph and every line it repeats on
    And removing all but one copy clears the report

  # BL-873 docs-duplicate-paragraph-03
  Scenario Outline: a short repeated line is not a duplicated paragraph
    Given a scanned docs tree whose markdown repeats the short line "<short_line>"
    When the duplicate-paragraph guard scans that tree
    Then it reports zero repeated paragraphs

    Examples:
      | short_line |
      | ---        |
      | ## Gaps    |

  # BL-873 docs-duplicate-paragraph-04
  Scenario: deduplication removes copies and nothing else
    Given the specification as it stood before deduplication
    When it is compared with the deduplicated specification
    Then every distinct paragraph of the original appears exactly once in the result
    And their relative order is unchanged

  # BL-873 docs-duplicate-paragraph-05
  Scenario: the surviving copy is the correct variant, not the most numerous one
    Given a paragraph that was duplicated in two textual variants
    When one copy is kept
    Then the kept copy is the variant whose shell example is correctly quoted
